{
  "slug": "work-unit-roadmap",
  "name": "Work Unit Roadmap",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "An AI agent workflow for professional software development using roadmap-driven execution, atomic Work Units, verification evidence, and one verified commit per completed unit. It helps AI coding agents plan, implement, test, review, and recover work with clean Git history, strict scope control, and full traceability across every phase.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **3 skills** and **7 commands**.\n\n- **Skills** (3): `using-git-worktrees` (Use when a WUR contract has executable project work that requires editing project files in a sparse worktree…), `using-wur` (Use when starting any conversation — establishes how to find and use WUR skills, requiring this bootstrap before…), `wur-guidelines` (Use when planning, tracking, contracting, receiving reports, or closing Work Unit Roadmap work)\n- **Commands** (7): `abort` (Abort an active phase — mark phase aborted, preserve trace, and stop contract execution), `done` (Client confirms phase complete — validate contract reports, update wiki, mark phase done), `init` (Bootstrap the agents/ workspace — create project philosophy, usage, and empty roadmap), `start` (Start or refresh a WUR execution contract for a phase), `status` (Show current project state — active phase, contract, WU, and wiki health), `test` (Record phase test status or create/update a failed execution round in the phase contract), `upgrade` (Upgrade an existing agents/ workspace to the schema this WUR plugin expects)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install work-unit-roadmap@claude-community` from `truong170201/work-unit-roadmap`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
